<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  Apple's privacy manifest, required for App Store submission.

  Universal Converter converts files on the phone and sends nothing (PRIVACY.md). Files
  are read in the app, the results are saved through the share sheet
  (@unisim/media/save: @capacitor/filesystem writes to the app's cache, then
  @capacitor/share), and they are gone when the app closes.

  No accounts (src/main.tsx `noAccounts: true`, no sign-in, no <UsageTracker />)
  and no suite user count from the phone app: the SDK's presence heartbeat (a
  random install id + platform every 45 s) is switched off in the iOS/Android
  shell (src/main.tsx `presence: !Capacitor.isNativePlatform()`), because the
  App Store and Play figures already count installs. The website still sends
  it; this manifest does not cover the website. So no data is collected, and
  nothing is used for tracking. The only network requests are the changelog
  (changelog.unisim.co.uk) and the app's own update check, neither of which
  carries anything about the user.

  Required-reason APIs: @capacitor/filesystem's native code reads file
  creation and modification dates (its `stat`), only for files in the app's
  own container, and the plugin ships no manifest of its own, so C617.1 is
  declared here. Capacitor's core frameworks carry their own manifests.

  Keep this in step with store-assets/data-safety.json, the App Store Connect
  privacy answers ("Data Not Collected") and PRIVACY.md. Written 2026-10-12
  (privacy audit).
-->
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<!-- @capacitor/filesystem: files in the app container. C617.1. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>C617.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
